{
  "about": "What a chat's lines become as people use them (spec/chat.md). pins (Pins, Polls, Editing and unsending): a chat's `lines` by id in order, its `pins` the latest first, then one `step`: pin or unpin a line, unsend one (送信取消), or settle the poll a line carries (日にちを決める). `expected` is the pins after it, the latest first, and the one that made room for the new pin (`dropped`, for the app to say so), if any. The most pinned at once is design/src/chat.ts's chatRules.maxPins, 5. edited (Editing and unsending): a line with words and its link's page is given new words; `expected` says whether it keeps its page (`kept`) or takes the new words' (`new`). firstUnread (Unread lines and typing): who wrote each line, oldest first (`others`, `me`, or `app` for the app's own lines such as someone joining), and how many are unread; `expected` is the index of the line the chat opens on under ここから新着, null with nothing unread. Only others' lines count. directThread (One-to-one chats, spec/sync-protocol.md): two members' ids, given in either order; `expected` is their chat's thread id, the same from both sides: \"direct:\" and the two ids in order (by their UTF-16 code units, as every id is ASCII), joined by \":\". openingFrom (Unread lines and typing): the first line a chat lays out as it opens, from its `latest` line's seq and the reader's `read` mark (null for no reader): its latest page, back to the first unread line when that is earlier, at most chatRules.openMax lines (pageSize 50, openMax 200). firstComing (Unread lines and typing): when lines come in while the chat is open and following, the first of them it stops at under ここから新着 rather than going past: of the chat's `lines` (each a seq and who wrote it, as firstUnread counts them), the first after both the `latest` line it held before and the reader's `read` mark that others wrote; `expected` is its seq, null for none. Whether to stop there or go on to the foot is the screen's: when they fit, it goes on. readTo (Unread lines and typing): what the reader's `read` mark comes to as the chat's `lines` (each a seq and who wrote it, as firstUnread counts them) show: `shown` are the seqs of those whose foot is on the screen, in no particular order; `expected.read` is the mark after, the latest of them, never back (a line once on screen stays read), and `expected.unread` how many of others' lines are still unread past it, what ↓ counts. draft (Drafts): what was being written in a chat, its `text` as it would be sent (mentions as <@id>), the line it answers (`replyTo`) or changes (`editing`) by seq, and the chat's `lines` the device holds then; `expected` is the draft kept, or opened again, or null when there is none to keep. withdrawn (Notifications): the chat lines' notifications a device has shown, each its `id`, chat (`groupId`, `threadId`) and line `seq`, and a `read` of one chat: its `readTo`, or null when the chat has no unread lines left; `expected` are the ids of those it takes back, in the order shown: the chat's, at or before readTo, all of the chat's for null. Another chat's, or a group's of the same thread name, stay.",
  "pins": [
    {
      "name": "a pinned line comes first among the pins",
      "lines": ["a", "b"],
      "pins": ["a"],
      "step": {
        "pin": "b"
      },
      "expected": {
        "pins": ["b", "a"],
        "dropped": null
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "one pin past the most takes the place of the oldest",
      "lines": ["p0", "p1", "p2", "p3", "p4", "new"],
      "pins": ["p4", "p3", "p2", "p1", "p0"],
      "step": {
        "pin": "new"
      },
      "expected": {
        "pins": ["new", "p4", "p3", "p2", "p1"],
        "dropped": "p0"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "pinning a line already pinned only moves it up",
      "lines": ["p0", "p1", "p2", "p3", "p4"],
      "pins": ["p4", "p3", "p2", "p1", "p0"],
      "step": {
        "pin": "p0"
      },
      "expected": {
        "pins": ["p0", "p4", "p3", "p2", "p1"],
        "dropped": null
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "taking a pin off leaves the others",
      "lines": ["a", "b"],
      "pins": ["b", "a"],
      "step": {
        "unpin": "b"
      },
      "expected": {
        "pins": ["a"],
        "dropped": null
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a line taken back is not among the pins",
      "lines": ["a", "b"],
      "pins": ["b", "a"],
      "step": {
        "unsend": "a"
      },
      "expected": {
        "pins": ["b"],
        "dropped": null
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a settled poll is pinned, within the most pins",
      "lines": ["p0", "p1", "p2", "p3", "p4", "poll"],
      "pins": ["p4", "p3", "p2", "p1", "p0"],
      "step": {
        "settle": "poll"
      },
      "expected": {
        "pins": ["poll", "p4", "p3", "p2", "p1"],
        "dropped": "p0"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "settling a pinned poll again only moves its pin up",
      "lines": ["poll", "p0", "p1", "p2", "p3"],
      "pins": ["p3", "p2", "p1", "p0", "poll"],
      "step": {
        "settle": "poll"
      },
      "expected": {
        "pins": ["poll", "p3", "p2", "p1", "p0"],
        "dropped": null
      }
    }
  ],
  "edited": [
    {
      "name": "an edit keeps its link's page while the link stays",
      "text": "ここ https://cafe.example",
      "edit": "ここどう？ https://cafe.example",
      "expected": "kept"
    },
    {
      "name": "a second link added after the first keeps the first's page",
      "text": "https://cafe.example",
      "edit": "https://cafe.example か https://b.example",
      "expected": "kept"
    },
    {
      "name": "an edit that changes the link takes the new page",
      "text": "https://cafe.example",
      "edit": "https://b.example",
      "expected": "new"
    },
    {
      "name": "a new link put before the old one takes the new page",
      "text": "https://cafe.example",
      "edit": "https://b.example じゃなくて https://cafe.example",
      "expected": "new"
    },
    {
      "name": "an edit that removes the link takes the new words' page, none",
      "text": "ここ https://cafe.example",
      "edit": "やっぱりいいや",
      "expected": "new"
    }
  ],
